# Scratch scripts written during a session: run once, then deleted. A failure part-way
# through one has three times left it behind for `git add -A` to sweep into a commit, which
# then took an `--amend` to undo. Ignoring them at the root makes that accident harmless
# instead of depending on remembering to check `git status` for a file I just wrote.
/_*.py
/_*.ts
